("art.room-to-grow.v1", "prompt", "Create a refined editorial illustration for a Christian article addressed to teenagers titled Room to Grow. Wide landscape aspect ratio 3:2, no text or lettering. Hand-painted gouache and fine coloured-pencil texture on warm cream paper, contemporary literary magazine quality, sophisticated not childish. One small young teenager seen from behind, gender ambiguous, casual everyday clothes, carrying a sketchbook, standing comfortably at a gently branching sandy path through low coastal grasses and a kitchen garden toward a calm blue-green ocean in morning light. A low stone garden wall, one small sapling, open airy sky; human figure is small within welcoming landscape. Soft warm earth, terracotta, sage, muted teal and honey daylight palette. Strong natural composition, generous breathing space, tactile organic shapes, restrained detail. Quiet curiosity and freedom to learn, no heroic pose, no halos or religious symbols, no school uniforms, no photographs, no dramatic danger, no arrows, no UI, no words. This is an imagined general scene, not a portrait of a real child.")
